          ],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "causing some paralysis of the bladder and causing spasms of the urinary sphincter.",
              "b": false
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "( opposite of sphincter incompetence). This occurs when there are lesions along the lumbar sacral regions (",
              "b": false
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "Rx: you need two drugs to successfully treat",
              "b": false
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "1) Urecholine (bethanecol) to contract bladder so it can empty instead of overflowing urine",
              "b": false
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "2) Prazosin or similar alpha blocker to relax urinary sphincter",
              "b": false
            }
          ],
          [],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "2 entirely different conditions for dribbling urine in male dogs",
              "b": true
            }
          ],
          [],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "1) Sphincter dyssnergia...due to neurological damage to the bladder and sphincter",
              "b": false
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "causing paralysis of the bladder wall and spasms of the urinary sphincter....get",
              "b": false
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "overflow incontinence and dribbling of urine",
              "b": false
            }
          ],
          [],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "2) Male incompetence of the urinary sphincter....due to weakness in the ability",
              "b": false
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "of the sphincter to hold back urine ( this is the opposite of sphincter dyssnergia",
              "b": false
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "treat with drugs that improve sphincter control...ie hormones, alpha 1 agonists like PPA",
              "b": false
            }
          ],
          [],
          [
            {
              "c": 1,
              "t": "Most times it is the first cause in male dogs especially older ones",
